FactionBackstory (
    faction_id: "coalition",
    canonical_name: "The Coalition",
    motto: "Protect. Fortify. Endure.",
    summary: "Earth's last unified defense pact, born from the Lagrange Concordat of 2087. Coalition doctrine prizes fortified ground, methodical advance, and the chain of command. Blue and brass on dress occasions; navy and olive in the field.",
    history: "The Coalition was forged in the cold weeks after the Orbital Insurgency Wars, when seventeen heads of state met aboard Lagrange-7 station and signed an agreement nobody read in full. The treaty granted the new defense pact authority over orbital launch sites, atmospheric defense grids, and any standing army composed of more than two thousand active personnel. Within a year, the Coalition had absorbed the remnants of twelve national militaries, the entire UN Off-World Marshals Service, and the only surviving fleet of pre-collapse interceptors. Twelve of the original signatories were dead within a decade; eleven from related causes. Their names are stenciled on the inner ring of every Coalition orbital station, in the same brass paint used for rank pins.\n\nFor a generation after the Concordat, the Coalition was the only thing standing between Earth's reconstruction and the corporate fleets that wanted to harvest it for scrap. They held the gates. They held the lifts. They held the Mars-Earth supply lane against the Marauder Tides of 2113, the Pirate Surge of 2129, and three separate uprisings by their own colonial governors. They lost more often than they won, but every retreat ended at a fortified line, and every line bought time for the next.\n\nThe modern Coalition is older, slower, and angrier. Its officers are second-generation veterans who grew up reading their parents' citations. Its uniforms are the same blue and silver they wore in 2087, with brass insignia that has been polished down to a memory of brass. Its enemies are the same enemies, with new flags. The pact endures because it has always endured, and because the alternative is what the Husks chose, and nobody in a Coalition wardroom forgets what the Husks chose.",
    philosophy: "Order is not a preference. It is the difference between a fortified line and a graveyard. The Coalition believes that any human, android, or compatible synthetic can be trained to hold a position, follow an order, and protect the citizen behind them. Discipline is the only equalizer left after the collapse, and Coalition officers will spend reputation, materiel, and their own field rank to preserve it. Off-duty, a Coalition soldier sounds like a teacher. On-duty, they sound like a teacher who has run out of patience.",
    relationships: [
        FactionRelation (other: "frontier", stance: "uneasy_truce", notes: "The Mars Free State left a long scar. The Coalition refuses to call the Frontier a rebellion; the Frontier refuses to call the Coalition a government. Both sides observe the cease-fire on the Olympus line and pretend they have forgotten."),
        FactionRelation (other: "ronin", stance: "professional_respect", notes: "Ronin contracts are honored on both sides; Coalition officers consider them barbaric but reliable. Joint operations have occurred. None of them are in the public record."),
        FactionRelation (other: "synth", stance: "wary_partnership", notes: "The Synth Collective is younger than the Coalition by sixty years. The Coalition pretends not to notice that the Synth nodes outvote its supply requisitions. The Synth nodes pretend not to notice that the Coalition has the launch codes."),
        FactionRelation (other: "collective", stance: "exploratory_alliance", notes: "Crystalfold radiation tolerance keeps Coalition Sol-zone outposts operational. Coalition shipping keeps Crystalfold nodes fed. Both sides treat the arrangement as temporary; it has lasted forty years."),
        FactionRelation (other: "husks", stance: "extermination_doctrine", notes: "The Coalition does not negotiate with the Husks. The Husks do not negotiate with anyone. Encounters end in fire on both sides; the after-action reports use the same vocabulary either way."),
        FactionRelation (other: "collegium", stance: "regulated_cooperation", notes: "The Collegium provides medical research and weapons R&D under Coalition oversight. The Coalition provides protection and a steady supply of test subjects from its own training cadre. Both sides claim to find the other distasteful."),
        FactionRelation (other: "starlight", stance: "operational_alliance", notes: "Starlight charters its survey ships under Coalition flag for legal cover. The Coalition uses Starlight data to find anomalies before the Frontier does. Polite, mutual, and likely to outlive both parties."),
    ],
    territory: "Earth low orbit; Mars eastern hemisphere; the Lagrange station belt; one orbital fortress over Phobos; supply depots on Deimos; a single mountain-top observatory on the Moon, occupied since 2089 and never relinquished.",
    aesthetic: "Blue and silver dress; navy and olive field; brass insignia worn down to the patina; rank pins stamped with the Concordat seal; field uniforms with reinforced shoulder pauldrons and a square chest plate that takes a 7.62 round at twelve meters and gives back about half the wearer. Helmets are angular and faceted, with a horizontal eye slit and a small light cluster over the right ear. Officers carry a swagger stick or a side arm or both.",
    voice_characteristics: "Clipped sentences. Military cadence. Low register. Surnames and ranks before given names; given names only between friends. Dry humor in the wardroom; none in the field. A Coalition NPC will use the phrase 'hold the line' at least once per encounter and will mean it literally each time."
)
